  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: ClinComm 3
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: "During a planning meeting for a clinical trial, you share concerns that
    you\u2019ve heard from patients about travel time, potential side effects, and
    time away from work. \n\n<b>In this situation, what role does the community advocate
    play in clinical trials?</b>"
  explanation: Community advocates serve as a bridge between patients and researchers
    by bringing real-life concerns into trial planning. When advocates share feedback
    about travel, side effects, or time commitments, they help teams design studies
    that are more realistic for patient participants. This helps remove barriers
    that might otherwise discourage patients from joining.
  correctAnswer: Sharing patient perspectives to shape how the trial is designed
  incorrectAnswer1: Choosing the trial treatment dose with the research team
  incorrectAnswer2: Reviewing the preclinical research data and approving the study
  incorrectAnswer3: Managing clinical trial data and communicating findings to the
    public
  questionRole: Community Advocate
  questionType: MultipleChoice
  questionStage: Clinical
